The fresh false-postcondition probe built successfully, then failed with exit 1 and `WarnStuckClaimState` at the actual `IntV(0)` result for `[]`; the mutation was reachable and semantically discriminating. Static review found no answer-smuggling oracle or proof-local execution bridge—the summaries are exhaustive mathematical functions—but the generated call/return semantics demonstrably converts two real `RecursionError` executions into normal results. I’m now consolidating the seven-stage trust accounting and verdict.
